    {
      "criterion": "E_opposite_support_survives_runtime",
      "result": "PASS_WITHIN_EXAMINED_CAPTURE_SCOPE",
      "observation": "Rendered run_0:0 shows the large near anatomical RIGHT foot low/planted and the far LEFT leg raised back. Rendered run_0:3 shows the near RIGHT knee/foot lifted near the body while the smaller far LEFT foot is low. The actual opposite source support change survives Godot rendering; the former repeated near-foot0/3 sequence is not what these captures show."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "E_direction_and_axe",
      "result": "PASS_FIRST_RUNTIME_SCREEN",
      "observation": "All six E RUN samples face SCREEN RIGHT with a lateral torso/overlapping shoulders. The same near RIGHT arm keeps the axe grip; no mirroring, opposite-facing frame, introduced wings or replacement body is visible."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "RUN_scale_and_clipping",
      "result": "NO_OBVIOUS_NEW_DEFECT_OBSERVED",
      "observation": "Across the six rendered E poses, body/armor proportions remain comparable while knees and torso compress/extend. No obvious abrupt scale doubling/shrinking, camera reversal, severed foot/horn/axe, or viewport-edge truncation was observed in the actual captures. The full 960x640 E0/E3 screenshots also show ample space around the complete figure."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "representative_transitions",
      "result": "NO_OBVIOUS_SEVERE_TRANSITION_DEFECT_OBSERVED",
      "observation": "Pre-idle to the sampled E RUN, representative E attack/hit poses and their captured return to idle retain the same boss identity and general displayed size. Attack lunges widen/lower the silhouette and hit recoils, without an observed catastrophic rescale or opposite-direction flip. E idle exposes more frontal chest/belt than the new lateral RUN; this residual pose-angle difference is recorded rather than treated as a newly invented runtime gate."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "S_and_NW_preservation",
      "result": "PASS_WITHIN_REPRESENTATIVE_CAPTURES",
      "observation": "S pre-idle and RUN0/3 stay front-facing, retain red heavy demon/axe identity, and visibly switch the low leg between the compared S RUN poses. NW pre-idle and RUN0/3 keep the back-left silhouette, tail and far RIGHT-hand axe/near empty LEFT-hand presentation. No obvious new direction/scale/truncation change was observed in these representatives. This is not an all-view gait approval."
    }
